# skills-submodule-update.install — this hook's install-hook.sh arguments.
#
# Read by .skills/doctor.sh (#224). When the doctor finds a hook symlink with no
# SessionStart registration, this is the line it prints as the repair. It lives
# beside the hook rather than in a table inside doctor.sh so that a skill adding
# a hook adds a manifest, not an edit to a script in another skill — the
# constants belong next to the hook they configure, which is where #200 put
# them.
#
# Format: the first line that is neither blank nor a comment is the argument
# list, appended to a resolved `bash <vendor>/…/install-hook.sh`. One line, and
# bounded to [A-Za-z0-9._-] and spaces, because it is printed into a command an
# operator is invited to paste.
#
# --label and --note are deliberately absent. They are install-refresh.sh's:
# --label renames the voice the installer speaks in, and this line is pasted at
# install-hook.sh, which is the name it would then be speaking under. Neither
# changes which artifacts land. install-refresh.sh remains the path README.md,
# docs/SKILLS.md and the #167 per-repo issues name; it is simply no longer a
# string the doctor derives from a hook it has just discovered.
--hook skills-submodule-update.sh --skill managing-skills
